      "heading": "The prosecution's case",
      "id": "P003",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "Prosecution counsel Reynaldo Robles said Dep-Ed submitted Army certifications to C O A as support for fifteen point five four million pesos reportedly paid as rewards. The prosecution argued that documents about programs conducted by the Army and local governments had been used to justify Dep-Ed spending. Colonel Manaros M. Boransing the Second supervised the First Infantry Division's civil-military activities."
    },
