      "heading": "The limits of Boransing's testimony",
      "id": "P005",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "Questioned by senator-judges, Boransing said his division received no confidential or surveillance information from Dep-Ed. He described its inputs as open-source information about students and available schools. He said he was not an intelligence officer and could not assess whether a standard activity certification established a link among informer information, a successful activity, and a reported reward. He also said he did not know how much Dep-Ed spent on the activities."
    },
