      "heading": "The defense position and burden of proof",
      "id": "P007",
      "kind": "finding",
      "text": "The defense agreed to stipulate that the three proposed A F P witnesses would testify that no confidential funds were transferred agency-to-agency for the activities. It refused to stipulate that no confidential information was shared, or that the officers did not know how the documents would be used. Lead defense counsel Sheila C. Sison pointed to language about Dep-Ed collaboration and information. After the prosecution invoked a prima facie presumption of misappropriation, the presiding officer clarified that the burden of proof remained with the prosecution."
    },
